window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-03d337741f7199f7"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"run-a-deep-security-scan\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">运行深度安全扫描</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾追加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>深度扫描会针对同一代码库或文件夹运行多次相互独立的标准扫描，并汇总其发现项。当你需要重复审查且可以接受更长运行时间和更多令牌用量时，可以使用深度扫描。</p> <p>先运行一次<a href=\"#/article/a-52ffdad46ad27a2b\">标准扫描</a>，确认扫描范围和安全上下文符合目标。重复审查可能发现先前扫描遗漏的问题，但不能保证发现所有问题，也不能保证每次运行结果完全一致。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-between-standard-and-deep-scans\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">在标准扫描和深度扫描之间选择</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th></th> <th>标准扫描</th> <th>深度扫描</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>审查方式</td> <td>一次标准扫描</td> <td>多次标准扫描并汇总发现项</td> </tr> <tr> <td>适用场景</td> <td>首次扫描或审查已定义的范围</td> <td>对该范围进行额外的独立审查</td> </tr> <tr> <td>扫描范围</td> <td>代码库或文件夹</td> <td>代码库或文件夹</td> </tr> <tr> <td>代码更改</td> <td>使用变更审查工作流</td> <td>不支持</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"start-the-deep-scan\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">启动深度扫描</h2> <p>为获得较好的扫描质量，请使用 <code>gpt-5.6-sol</code>，并选择 <code>xhigh</code> 推理强度。</p> <ol> <li>打开 <strong>Security（安全）</strong> &gt; <strong>Scans（扫描）</strong>，然后选择 <strong>+ Scan（新建扫描）</strong>。</li> <li>选择一个代码库或文件夹，选择 <strong>Codebase（代码库）</strong>，并开启 <strong>Deep scan（深度扫描）</strong>。扫描会审查所选的整个代码库或文件夹。</li> <li>选择模型和推理强度。在 <strong>Additional context（补充上下文）</strong>中添加威胁模型或部署环境信息。</li> <li>选择 <strong>Start scan（开始扫描）</strong>。</li> </ol> <p>你也可以从 Codex 对话中启动扫描：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $codex-security:deep-security-scan to run a deep security scan of this repository.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">使用 $codex-security:deep-security-scan，对这个代码仓库运行深度安全扫描。</div></div> <p>如果只扫描一个组件，请将“this repository”替换为该文件夹的路径。</p> <p>深度扫描工作进程会继承你选择的模型和推理设置。每个工作进程都会运行一次完整的标准扫描，Codex Security 会汇总已完成的结果。你可以在 <strong>Scans（扫描）</strong>中查看已保存的扫描，也可以选择 <strong>View activity（查看活动）</strong>打开对应的 Codex 任务。如果需要限制并发量或运行时长，请在启动前设置<a href=\"#/article/a-03d337741f7199f7?anchor=configure-deep-scan-runtime\">运行时间限制</a>。</p> <blockquote> <p>截图未离线保存: Codex Security 工作台显示深度扫描及其正在进行的审查阶段</p> </blockquote> <figcaption> 跟踪深度扫描当前阶段；审阅最终结果前，可以先查看对应的 Codex 活动。 </figcaption> <p><a id=\"review-the-result\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">审阅结果</h2> <p>深度扫描与标准扫描一样，会保存扫描详情和完整扫描目录。在 <strong>Scans（扫描）</strong>中打开已完成的扫描，或在 <strong>Findings（发现项）</strong>中查看其发现项。如果你要求生成详细漏洞报告或结构性加固指导，生成的 <code>report.md</code> 会链接到这些内容。 分享或归档结果时，请将相关的 <code>findings/</code> 和 <code>hardening/</code> 目录与报告放在一起。</p> <p>请先查看覆盖范围摘要，再审阅发现项。深度扫描仍有局限，因此在得出结论前，请检查延期处理的范围和剩余证据缺口。对于你认可的发现项，请继续阅读<a href=\"#/article/a-44471eb3eae1b363\">修复并验证发现项</a>。</p> <p>若要审查拉取请求、提交、分支范围或本地补丁，请使用<a href=\"#/article/a-06694345b68735af\">审查代码更改</a>。深度扫描不接受差异作为扫描目标。</p> <p><a id=\"configure-deep-scan-runtime\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">配置深度扫描运行参数</h2> <p>若要控制深度扫描的并发量和时长，请创建或编辑 <code>~/.codex/codex-security/config.toml</code>。如果设置了 <code>CODEX_HOME</code>，则改为使用 <code>$CODEX_HOME/codex-security/config.toml</code>。</p> <p>例如，下面的配置可以缩短扫描时间并限制并发量：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">[deep_scan]\nworkers = 2\nsubagents = 0\nstop_after_no_new = 3\nmax_discovery_runs = 10\nmax_time_hours = 1.5\n</code></pre> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>设置</th> <th>默认值</th> <th>说明</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>workers</code></td> <td><code>4</code></td> <td>允许同时运行的独立标准扫描工作进程数。旧版的 <code>\"auto\"</code> 也会解析为 <code>4</code>。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>subagents</code></td> <td><code>3</code></td> <td>每个工作进程可启动的子代理数量。设为 <code>0</code> 可禁用子代理。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>stop_after_no_new</code></td> <td><code>4</code></td> <td>连续完成这么多次工作进程扫描且没有产生新发现项后停止。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>stop_after_consecutive_errors</code></td> <td><code>3</code></td> <td>连续出现这么多次工作进程错误后停止。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>max_discovery_runs</code></td> <td><code>40</code></td> <td>限制汇总前运行的独立标准扫描次数。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>max_time_hours</code></td> <td><code>96</code></td> <td>将工作进程的最长运行时间限制为正数，最多 <code>96</code> 小时；也可以按需使用小数。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>较低的数值可以减少扫描时间和令牌用量，但也可能漏掉发现项。配置更改仅对新启动的深度扫描生效，不会改变正在运行的扫描。</p> <p>达到时间限制后，Codex Security 会停止未完成的工作进程，保留已完成的扫描结果，并将这些结果汇总到最终报告中。如果在截止时间前没有工作进程完成源代码审查，报告会注明覆盖范围不完整。</p> <p><code>max_time_hours</code> 设置要求插件版本为 <code>0.1.19</code> 或更高。有关版本信息，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-796d8353993fb17e\">插件更新日志</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"run-a-deep-security-scan\">Run a deep security scan</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>A deep scan runs multiple independent standard scans over the same repository or folder and combines their findings. Use it when you want repeated review and can allow for the additional runtime and token use.</p> <p>Start with a <a href=\"#/article/a-52ffdad46ad27a2b\">standard scan</a> to check that the scope and security context match your goal. Repeated review can find issues missed by an earlier pass, but doesn't guarantee complete detection or identical results between runs.</p> <h2 id=\"choose-between-standard-and-deep-scans\">Choose between standard and deep scans</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th></th> <th>Standard scan</th> <th>Deep scan</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Review</td> <td>One standard scan</td> <td>Multiple standard scans with combined findings</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Use it for</td> <td>A first scan or a review of a defined scope</td> <td>Additional independent reviews of that scope</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Scope</td> <td>Repository or folder</td> <td>Repository or folder</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Changes</td> <td>Use the change-review workflow</td> <td>Not supported</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"start-the-deep-scan\">Start the deep scan</h2> <p>For the best scan quality, use <code>gpt-5.6-sol</code> with <code>xhigh</code> reasoning effort.</p> <ol> <li>Open <strong>Security</strong> &gt; <strong>Scans</strong> and select <strong>+ Scan</strong>.</li> <li>Choose a repository or folder, select <strong>Codebase</strong>, and turn on <strong>Deep scan</strong>. The scan reviews the entire selected repository or folder.</li> <li>Choose the model and reasoning effort. Add threat-model or deployment context under <strong>Additional context</strong>.</li> <li>Select <strong>Start scan</strong>.</li> </ol> <p>You can also start it from a Codex conversation:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $codex-security:deep-security-scan to run a deep security scan of this repository.\n</code></pre> <p>For one component, replace \"this repository\" with the path to its folder.</p> <p>Deep scan workers inherit your selected model and reasoning settings. Each worker runs a complete standard scan, and Codex Security aggregates the completed results. Follow the saved scan from <strong>Scans</strong>, or select <strong>View activity</strong> to inspect its Codex task. Set <a href=\"#/article/a-03d337741f7199f7?anchor=configure-deep-scan-runtime\">runtime limits</a> before starting if you need to limit concurrency or duration.</p> <blockquote> <p>Screenshot not stored offline: Native Codex Security workbench showing a deep scan and its active review phase</p> </blockquote> <figcaption> Track the active deep-scan phase and inspect its Codex activity before reviewing the completed result. </figcaption> <h2 id=\"review-the-result\">Review the result</h2> <p>Deep scans use the same saved scan details and complete scan directory as standard scans. Open the completed scan in <strong>Scans</strong> or review its findings in <strong>Findings</strong>. The generated <code>report.md</code> links to detailed vulnerability reports or structural hardening guidance when you request those outputs. Keep any linked <code>findings/</code> and <code>hardening/</code> directories with the report when sharing or archiving the result.</p> <p>Review the coverage summary before the findings. Even a deep scan has limits, so check deferred surfaces and remaining proof gaps before drawing a conclusion. For a finding you accept, continue with <a href=\"#/article/a-44471eb3eae1b363\">Fix and verify a finding</a>.</p> <p>To review a pull request, commit, branch range, or local patch, use <a href=\"#/article/a-06694345b68735af\">Review code changes</a>. Deep scans don't accept diff targets.</p> <h2 id=\"configure-deep-scan-runtime\">Configure deep-scan runtime</h2> <p>To control a deep scan's concurrency and duration, create or edit <code>~/.codex/codex-security/config.toml</code>. If you set <code>CODEX_HOME</code>, use <code>$CODEX_HOME/codex-security/config.toml</code> instead.</p> <p>For example, this profile runs a shorter scan with limited concurrency:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">[deep_scan]\nworkers = 2\nsubagents = 0\nstop_after_no_new = 3\nmax_discovery_runs = 10\nmax_time_hours = 1.5\n</code></pre> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Setting</th> <th>Default</th> <th>Description</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>workers</code></td> <td><code>4</code></td> <td>Number of independent standard-scan workers allowed to run at the same time. Legacy <code>\"auto\"</code> also resolves to <code>4</code>.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>subagents</code></td> <td><code>3</code></td> <td>Number of subagents each worker may start. Set <code>0</code> to disable them.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>stop_after_no_new</code></td> <td><code>4</code></td> <td>Stop after this many consecutive completed worker scans produce no new findings.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>stop_after_consecutive_errors</code></td> <td><code>3</code></td> <td>Stop after this many consecutive worker errors.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>max_discovery_runs</code></td> <td><code>40</code></td> <td>Limit the number of independent standard-scan runs before aggregation.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>max_time_hours</code></td> <td><code>96</code></td> <td>Limit worker execution to a positive number of hours up to <code>96</code>; use fractions as needed.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Lower values can reduce scan time and token use but may miss findings. Configuration changes apply to new deep scans, not scans already in progress.</p> <p>When the time limit expires, Codex Security stops unfinished workers, keeps completed scan results, and aggregates them into the final report. If no worker finishes source review before the deadline, the report records partial coverage.</p> <p>The <code>max_time_hours</code> setting requires plugin version <code>0.1.19</code> or later. See the <a href=\"#/article/a-796d8353993fb17e\">plugin changelog</a> for release details.</p>"};
